WEBVTT

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.080
What happened?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.660
His daughter is sick.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:27.840
What's wrong?

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.410
I think she has a stomachache.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.100
He's a good father.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.080
So... what do you think of him?

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.860
He's very nice.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.220
But I think he was nervous tonight.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.000
It was his first date in two years.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.060
Will you see him again?

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.100
I hope so.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.380
This food is delicious.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.420
He didn't get a thing to eat.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.140
You ordered enough for three or four people,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.680
but I'm not complaining.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.500
Who is that?

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:15.960
Do you think it's...

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:25.360
No. You won't believe it, Marilyn!

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.900
I believe it. Even without looking.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.160
Hi!

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.300
How...?

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.440
Your downstairs neighbor let me in.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.840
Did you go home?

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.360
I did , but everything is OK,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.060
so I decided to come back.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.960
To apologize for leaving so early,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.860
I brought you a little gift.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.460
It's a bonsai tree for your new apartment.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.950
Hi, Marilyn. I hope it's not too late.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.500
Oh, not at all. We're still eating.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.660
Please, come in. Join us.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.840
It's our meal from the restaurant.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.040
And how is your daughter?

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.010
Oh, she's fine.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.240
It was only a tummy ache.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.400
It's good that you went back.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.960
Yes, I think it's important for me to

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.300
be there since her mother died.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.940
I agree. Aren't you hungry?

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.640
As a matter of fact... I am hungry.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.660
There's lots of food left.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.680
Mmm, this is delicious!

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:26.680
Enjoy!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.240
I'm going to excuse myself.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.440
I have a lot of work to do to get ready for tomorrow.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.570
Good night, Harry. It was nice meeting you.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.060
Bye, Marilyn.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.440
Good night, Susan.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.720
Good night, Marilyn.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.020
She's going to a fashion show here in the city tomorrow.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.300
so she won't have to travel from Riverdale in the morning.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:49.960
You two must be close.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.280
we are.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.700
The whole Stewart family is close.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.900
I like that.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.980
And then, two years ago, my wife died.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.140
You miss her.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.260
I do...yes, but I have Michelle...

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.300
and with time...

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.540
Is there anyone else in your life?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.040
No, not yet. What about you?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.680
Oh, I date occasionally,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.910
but my work keeps me busy.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.110
I have an early start tomorrow,

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.070
and the baby-sitter has to get home.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.120
Where did the time go?

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.300
It's midnight.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.300
Thank you, Susan.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.840
I had a nice evening.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.380
Me, too, Harry.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.220
Harry?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.020
Yes?

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.670
I'd like to meet your daughter someday.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.140
Does that mean that I can see you again?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.540
Of course.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.420
Wonderful. I'll call you,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.340
and we'll go out to dinner.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.520
Please do.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.100
I promise I won't leave early.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.860
It was for a good reason.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.260
You know something?

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.540
What?

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.380
I think we're going to be good friends.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.240
Good night, Susan.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:31.900
Good night, Harry,

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.460
Have a safe trip home.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:43.410
Are you all right?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.620
Sorry.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.020
I never liked that umbrella stand.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.460
Good night, Harry.
